@holistis, @hheskihoran - a short note rather than a pitch -

The part I’d pull out is the INFLATED-VALUE miss. A check that could not fire is not a check that passed, and reporting it as amount-unbound rather than valid is the whole point. It is the “not evaluated” outcome in my own work, so it is good to see it reached independently. The same goes for saying plainly that the receipt has exactly one independent party.

On bytes as transmitted versus a canonical re-serialisation: its worth settling up front. Our corpus is checked on the canonical form (JCS), and an independent cross-language h

@ogasurfproject-jpg's text above describes exactly a shape we've been running in production: "log consistency that independent witnesses can check," plus records created after the fact that the operator doesn't control.

Two things from implementation, not from this charter:

1. **Independent witnesses, right now.** We just did this, literally today, on @ogasurfproject-jpg's own pilot (ogasurfproject-jpg/horizon-shield#51): signed a set of acknowledgements over published items with a dedicated key, anchored them with OpenTimestamps, as an optional witness alongside the pilot's own threshold-2

